The answer is: ...came down from the mountain. They were hungry, and they saw a light in the sky. They went towards it and saw that it was a bonfire. They went towards the bonfire and saw that it was being tended by four old women. The women welcomed the men and fed them. The men then went to bed. In the morning, the women told the men that they had dreamed that the men had been killed by the police. The men then went to the village and told everyone what had happened. The police came and arrested the four old women. The women were sent to jail and the bonfire was extinguished.

This story is from the Ojibwe nation.


